{"id": "32441", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=32441", "title": "Shelby (Montana)", "text": "Shelby is an important town for commerce in north-central Montana. Around 3,100 people live there.\nGet in.\nBy car.\nShelby is at the intersection of Interstate 15 and U.S. Highway 2 (US-2), it's hard to miss. I-15 spans the entire state from north to south while US-2 spans the entire state east and west.\nThe Canadian border crossing at Sweet Grass is only 30 mi north on I-15. The crossing has the highest traffic volume in the state.\nGet around.\nThe historic Main Street Business District is easily walked. Many places will require a car."}
{"id": "32443", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=32443", "title": "Shelby (Ohio)", "text": "Shelby is a city in Richland County, in the state of Ohio, USA.\nDrink.\nThere are plenty of choices for alcohol. Most grocery stores carry it, as do the gas stations, drive-throughs and convenience stores."}
