{"id": "32446", "revid": "2200769", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=32446", "title": "Shelbyville (Illinois)", "text": "Shelbyville is a city in Central Illinois.\nUnderstand.\nThe dishwasher was invented here.\nGet in.\nBy plane.\nShelby County Airport\nBy train.\nAmtrak Stations are located in:\nBy car.\nIllinois state routes 16 &amp; 128 pass thru Shelbyville\nLocated in the approx center of interstates...\nI57 - 30 miles to the East\nI70 - 35 miles to the South\nI72 - 45 miles to the North\nI55 - 55 Miles to the West\nDo.\nFishing, Boating, Water Skiing, Swimming, Hunting, State and Federal parks for Camping, Golf, Bowling, Movies, Beaches"}
{"id": "32447", "revid": "2164467", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=32447", "title": "Shelbyville (Indiana)", "text": "Shelbyville is a small town in the Nine-County Region of Indiana."}
{"id": "32448", "revid": "2236161", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=32448", "title": "Shelbyville (Kentucky)", "text": "Shelbyville is a city in the Kentucky Derby Region, 30 mi east of Louisville and 20 mi west of Frankfort. It is the county seat of Shelby County.\nGet in.\nBy car.\nInterstate 64 crosses Shelby County from west to east, linking Shelbyville with Louisville and, eventually, St. Louis to the west. Eastbound traffic will go to Lexington and on to West Virginia and Virginia Beach. Exits along I-64 in Shelby County are Exit 28 (KY 1848, Veechdale Rd) at Simpsonville, Exit 32 (KY 55, Taylorsville-Shelbyville) and Exit 35 (KY 53) both at Shelbyville and Exit 43 (KY 395, Waddy-Petona).\nBy plane.\nLouisville International Airport offers numerous flights to cities around the country.\nCapitol City Airport in Frankfort handles small aircraft.\nDrink.\nAlcohol.\nShelby County is officially classified by the state's Department of Alcoholic Beverage Control as \"moist\", meaning that the county as a whole is \"dry\" (not allowing alcohol sales) but contains a \"wet\" city where full retail sales, both packaged and by the drink, are allowed. The city of Shelbyville is wet. The surrounding county is 'moist\" in a different sense, prohibiting package sales but allowing sales by the drink in larger restaurants (seating at least 100)."}
{"id": "32449", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=32449", "title": "Sheldon (Iowa)", "text": "Sheldon is in Western Iowa.\nGet in.\nMost people drive, but if you have your own plane, there's another option."}
{"id": "32450", "revid": "162256", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=32450", "title": "Shelkar", "text": "Shelkar is a town in Xigatse Prefecture.\nGet in.\nLocated 7 km off of the Friendship Hwy. Most travelers skip Shelkar and stay at the hotels near the Shelkar Junction, where the road to town meets the highway. There is no public transportation available.\nBuy.\nPetrochina has a filling station at the Junction\nEat.\nPricey food in the hotels and guesthouses. \nSleep.\nThe Everest Service Center Hotel sells the Everest Base Camp tickets which allow access to Qomolangma National Nature Reserve. Other places to stay are the Mt Everest Home Inn, Chengdu Jiudian, and the Shigar Snowland Hotel."}
{"id": "32451", "revid": "162256", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=32451", "title": "Shelley", "text": "Shelley is a town of 4,700 people (2019) in Southeastern Idaho known for its Spud Day festival.\nGet in.\nShelley is 8 miles (13 km) south of Idaho Falls on US 91."}
{"id": "32452", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=32452", "title": "Shellharbour", "text": "\"Minnamurra redirects here \u2013 see Budderoo National Park for the rainforest\"\nShellharbour is a coastal city of 76,271 (2021) in between Wollongong and the Shoalhaven, in the Illawarra region of New South Wales halfway between Wollongong and Kiama.\nUnderstand.\nShellharbour a satellite city of Wollongong, 85 km south of Sydney. It has a town centre that has civic buildings and the major shopping mall of Shellharbour Square. It has a township on the water, adjacent to a small harbour and a beach. Shell Cove is a major housing development adjacent to the town, and to the water.\nGet in.\nBy train.\nThe Kiama branch of the South Coast Line (SCO) has hourly services from Wollongong, Helensburgh and Sydney. While the alignment is slow and windy, the trains that make it to Shellharbour do end up following an express route north of Wollongong.\n is a commuter station with parking and a bus interchange - quite distant from facilities or towns. It really looks quite in the middle of nowhere getting off the train there. It is around a 4-km walk to Shellharbour town, going up and down a few hills.\n is outside the town, but quite close to the HARS Aircraft Museum.\nIf you want to get the bus into town, or to Shellharbour Square, a better bet may be to get off at and get a bus. They run with around a 2 hour frequency to town, and quite frequently to Shellharbour Square. Check the timetable, and get the first bus to Shellharbour Square if it makes sense to do so.\nBy bike.\nIf you are a keen cyclist, it is also a nice ride from Wollongong mostly along the coast.\nBy car.\nThe town is about 85 km and 2 hours' drive from Sydney. Go past the end of the freeway from Sydney, and Shellharbour town is off to your left, follow the signs. A scenic route goes via Wollongong and Warilla, and follows the water. Exit the freeway at Five Islands Road, follow the signs to Warilla at the second major right hand turn and on to Windang Rd, then follow your nose.\nGet around.\nThere are limited bus services, as well as three train stations.\nEat.\nBefore the Albion Park Rail Bypass of the Princes Mwy was built, traffic was essentially forced to use a short non-freeway section of highway in Albion Park between two freeways. This resulted in many fast-food chains such as Maccas, Subway, Oporto and Taco Bell in addition to local eateries to open up on the southbound section, which gave Albion Park an unusual amount of eateries. If you find it hard to find a good place in the city centre or if many of the restaurants close early (typical for Australia), many fast food chains will still be open in Albion Park."}
{"id": "32453", "revid": "162256", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=32453", "title": "Shell Knob", "text": "Shell Knob is a small town in the Southwest Missouri Ozarks and a lake resort community. It is located near the western edge of Tablerock Lake. Shell Knob is quiet small town, which sees a spike in activity during the summer holiday (Memorial Day, 4th of July, Labor Day) as the out of town lake visitors pour into town.\nGet in.\nHighway 39 runs North / South through Shell Knob. Located approx. 10 miles North of the Missouri / Arkansas border. Shell Knob sits on the western end of Tablerock Lake.\nThere is a small airport which will accommodate small airplanes.\nGet around.\nBy car as there is no public transportation.\nSee.\nThere are some beautiful back roads to drive on, some nice views of the lake.\nBuy.\nThere are a few small local shops that carry antiques / crafts."}
{"id": "32455", "revid": "36420", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=32455", "title": "Shelter Island", "text": "Shelter Island is an island and town in Suffolk County in New York. It is between the two forks on Long Island and in total is 6.5 sq miles and was founded by the Sylvester family.\nGet in.\nIn order to get onto this island, you must take either:\nGet around.\nThe main means of getting around on the island is by car. But you may also walk or ride a bike.\nBuy.\nThere are quite a few little shops on the island that are worth checking out. There are some antique shows, gifts shops, specialty shops, and a few delis, etc.\nThere is a newly owned IGA supermarket at 75 North Ferry Road, that offers home and boat delivery. Catering also available 631-749-0382.\nIf needed there are also two banks and two post offices.\nEat.\nThere are plenty of restaurants where you may want to grab a bite to eat.\nDrink.\nThere are quite a few places to get a drink. All the hotels have a bar and you can also get drinks at The Dory."}
